review:
This game is amazing, the core design, the creativity, the music, and the challenge, it is awesome and you will enjoy it. BUT, as this game hasn't been updated in 4 years, it gets boring fast. The developer is a incompetent dumbass who doesn't know how to manage a game. Between previous updates, he has showed great effort and creativity with each update, and at a quick notice to, but now, hes basically just a watered down Yandere Dev without the weird shit. If he truly liked this game, and wanted to support it, he would fix the many bugs, glitches, limitations, and optimize the game for future playing devices. On top of the community, where do I start, between 2015-2017 the community was pretty nice, drama here and there, got your levels that stand out and such, but now? Its a cess pool, got your groomers, sweats, etc. Want to make a good level to meet the community standards? Sorry cant, everyone is Funnygame now and basically a god at creating, so even if it is good, its just like the rest of the levels now and stale. Oh new hardest thing in the game, we have seen so many of that same shit over the years its boring, and because of that difficulty is the lifeline of the game. Star grinding, after michigun became number 2 it kinda became irrelevant sorry. Everyone now is so entitled to themselves, "If I did it, or made it and I said its good, its good" With no accepting Criticism or anything. If you can think of it its probably in the community of this game. You can meet some really cool people here and I mean it, but how it is at the time of this review, straight ass water, and with an update taking 4+ years no wonder this game would fall to such a low state. Unless people change their outlook on the game, it will continue to fall.

To Sum it up, game is great, awesome mechanics, amazing creators, so much freedom, but with a lack of Developer support where it relies on its own community to even fix its game, and the community itself being a freak show, I would not play this game for more then a year at most. But at the end I recommend it as it is still awesome but dont go to deep.


@Robtop if you see this shit, bro no one cares about 300 something new icons when people are gonna use the same mainstream ones since 2.0. I get it, new content, but sometimes the more important things such as managing, money, and other stuff comes into play. You can turn this game around.
